{
  "$description": "The light palette, resolving every semantic role to exactly one foundation token. THIS IS THE DEFAULT RENDERED THEME, and it is selected by the CSS class `.body.dark`. Read inversionWarning before using this file.",
  "themeId": "light",
  "isDefault": true,
  "selectedByCssClass": ".body.dark",
  "canvas": "white",
  "themes": {
    "light": "tokens/themes/light.json",
    "dark": "tokens/themes/dark.json"
  },
  "inversionWarning": "LOAD-BEARING AND COUNTER-INTUITIVE. The CSS class names for the two palettes are INVERTED:\n  .body            carries the DARK values  (src/styles/fourmula-base.css:2248-2265)\n  .body.dark       carries the LIGHT values (src/styles/fourmula-base.css:2273-2286)\nand the app ships <body class=\"body dark\"> (index.html:16). So the class literally named \"dark\" selects the LIGHT palette, and the DEFAULT RENDERED THEME IS LIGHT (white canvas). public/motion/m10.js reinforces this: it toggles the class 'dark', defaults to true, stores localStorage['isDarkMode'] and sets data-theme-state=\"dark\" on the toggle - all while the page renders light. A generator that treats '.body.dark' as the dark theme inverts the entire palette.",
  "imageInversion": "The inversion repeats at TWO MORE layers, and both matter. (1) Image classes: .theme-dark images ship visible (display:flex) and .theme-light images ship hidden, while the page renders LIGHT. (2) Asset filenames: the file shown in the default light rendering is the one whose name ends -dark.avif. public/motion/m11.js swaps the pair.",
  "observedAsymmetry": "public/motion/m11.js:20 initialises with document.body.classList.contains(\"light\"), but public/motion/m10.js only ever toggles the class 'dark' and never 'light', so that expression is always false. Its theme:changed listener (m11.js:22-24) uses the real boolean instead. The effect is a first-paint vs post-toggle asymmetry in which image of a theme pair is shown. The motion scripts are byte-identical copies of the original site's own scripts and are READ-ONLY, so this is recorded, not fixed.",
  "evidence": [
    "cit-theme-body-dark-palette",
    "cit-theme-body-dark-light-palette",
    "cit-theme-index-html",
    "cit-theme-m10-toggle",
    "cit-theme-m11-images",
    "cit-theme-asset-suffix"
  ],
